  "status_text": "Flip the answer once and seven parts do the work of ten. A contributor just ruled out doing it in six, even with as many flips as you like. Light one row and one column on a four-by-four board. Is their square marked? The bottom row is blank, along with one square in each other row. Spot those blanks and flip the answer. With AND and OR alone the board takes ten gates, each reading at most two wires. One NOT gate saves all three, the most any board this size allows under those rules (L-meta-25827, L-meta-25970, L-meta-6337, L-meta-25780).",
